# app              job                    endpoint             build-token
# (endpoint: build | buildWithParameters — yolo's job is parameterised)
#
# THIS FILE IS THE DEPLOY LIST. trigger-app-builds.sh reads its app column, in order,
# so adding a row here is all it takes to deploy an app. (Until 2026-08-07 the script
# also carried a hardcoded list, and a row added here alone did nothing.)
#
# ORDER MATTERS: yolo stays LAST. It is the heaviest pipeline, and monitoring/grafana
# hard-mounts two ConfigMaps that only the yolo deploy creates (grafana-alerting-yolo,
# grafana-dashboard-yolo-pipeline — see kube-prometheus manifests/YOLO-OWNERSHIP.md), so
# Grafana stays ContainerCreating until yolo lands.
#
# build-token: Jenkins' per-job remote-trigger token. jenkins-deploy-url.sh builds
#   https://<cred>@jenkins.../job/<job>/<endpoint>?token=<build-token>
# Because that URL carries the credential, the request is AUTHENTICATED and Jenkins only
# consults the token as the ANONYMOUS alternative — an authenticated user with Build
# permission is allowed through whatever the token says. So this column must be non-empty
# (jenkins-deploy-url.sh requires all four fields) but is not load-bearing here. Verified
# 2026-08-07: prop-investech has NO authToken in its config.xml at all, and QCX's is
# stored encrypted ({AQAAAB...}) so its plaintext cannot be recovered from Jenkins.
qcguy            qcguy                  build                qcguy
predictonomy     predictonomy           build                predict
bestrentaladmin  bestrentaladmin        build                best
dyingpaleblue    dyingpaleblue          build                dying
# aisucks added 2026-08-18 — the SAME bug this file's header describes, third instance.
# The Jenkins job `aisucks` has existed and worked for a while (builds */main, live at
# aisucks.qcguy.com with a running `aisucks` namespace), but it was never listed here, so
# no bootstrap and no DR run ever deployed it — exactly how qcx and prop-investech were
# found. It was ALSO missing from restore-lib.sh's clone manifest, so a bare-metal restore
# would neither clone nor deploy it: the site would simply not come back, with no error.
# Like prop-investech, this job has NO authToken in its config.xml; the 4th column must be
# non-empty but is not load-bearing (the request authenticates via JENKINS_CRED).
aisucks          aisucks                build                aisucks
ollama           ollama                 build                ollama
qcx              QCX                    build                qcx
prop-investech   prop-investech         build                prop-investech
yolo             trading-microservices  buildWithParameters  yolo
